CM_ SG_ 338 COM_CRC "Calculated over all header signals. From the signal after the CRC until the last signal in the message";
CM_ SG_ 338 COM_Protocol_Version "What version of this protocol we are up to";
CM_ SG_ 338 COM_Sync_Frame_ID "synchronizes between the messages in the same frame";
CM_ SG_ 338 COM_Frame_MCU_TS_Start "Timestamp of exposure start expressed in MCU time system";
CM_ SG_ 338 COM_Last_MCU_Sync_TS "Feedback of last clock sync timestamp that was sent to EyeQ from MCU";
CM_ SG_ 338 COM_Last_Clock_Sync_Skew "Skew between actual clock sync time that was sent to EyeQ and what EyeQ was expecting. If internal error exceeds signal limits, signal is clamped to its maximum.";
CM_ SG_ 338 COM_Last_Clock_Sync_Error "If Skew is larger than defined in configuration as error or data corruption was found this bit will be turned on to True";
CM_ SG_ 338 COM_EyeQ_Frame_ID "Index of the frame by frame processed number. Only images processed by algo are assigned a number hence the output will be sequential.";
CM_ SG_ 338 COM_Cam_Frame_ID "Actual grab index from camera. Not every image is processed by algo however. This may not be sequential as some are dropped. This is what the logger sees on the headers";
CM_ SG_ 338 COM_DayTime_Indicator "Check Enum Values";
CM_ SG_ 338 COM_Driving_Side_V "Validator set to false in case the signal is not available.";
CM_ SG_ 338 COM_Driving_Side "Indicates driving side.";
CM_ SG_ 338 COM_Is_HighSpeed_Road_V "Validator set to false in case the signal is not available.";
CM_ SG_ 338 COM_Is_HighSpeed_Road "TSR Responsibility: If detected, highway semantics and high driving speed signal will be set to true";
CM_ SG_ 338 Reserved_1 "Indicates in which FPS reporting cycle we are. The default mode is 36 FPS (0=REPORT_36) . When 9/18/36 FPS is enabled the signal will indicate (1=REPORT_9_18_36)";
CM_ SG_ 338 Reserved_2 "Indicate the protocol cycles of protocols in every frame. Reports all the output messages that can be reported in the frame, and not only the messages that are reported.";
CM_ SG_ 338 Reserved_3 "Indicate the protocol cycles of protocols in every frame. Reports all the output messages that can be reported in the frame, and not only the messages that are reported.";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Header_CRC "Calculated over all header signals. From the signal after the CRC until the first signal in the elements FS_CRC_0 not including";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Protocol_Version "Version number of failsafe message";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Sync_ID "The ID of the Sync message, used to synchronize between signals in the system. Every new frame promotes the sync ID by one.";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Cameras_Number "Number of FS available cameras";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_TSR_Out_OF_Calib "Specific TSR Out-of-Calib Signal";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Out_Of_Calib "Vision detected that the calibration camera to world exceede level 0 40 px tollerance  from the baseline calibration (Auto Fix).";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Impacted_Technologies "Impacted technologies from detected fail safes according to the fail-safe ME schema";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Rain "Detection of precipitation.";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Fog "Detection of fog.";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Calibration_Misalignment "Road Model misalignment";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_C2W_OOR "The Out Of Range (OOR) FS signal will indicate that the current Cam2World extrinsic calibration found exceeded the allowed system tolerance defined by the OEM using the min/max Yaw/Horizon and MaxRoll ranges definitions";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_CRC_0 "Calculated over all element signals. From the signal after the CRC until the first signal in the next elements FS_CRC_N+1  not including";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Camera_ID_0 "The relevant camera.";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Free_Sight_0 "False until free sight is approved";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Splashes_0 "The lower edges of vehicles cannot be detected due to water spray, a.k.a. splashes.";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Sun_Ray_0 "Strong glare due to micro scratches on windshield.";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Low_Sun_0 "Sun glare which disrupts the image. The sun appears over the FOE.";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Blur_Image_0 "Issued when visibility on the image is lowered such that detection of objects inside the Danger Zone (in-path and next lanes up-to some level) cannot be fully performed";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Partial_Blockage_0 "Low visibility due to partially covered lens.";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Full_Blockage_0 "No visibility due to fully covered lens. Takes 50 frames with no edges. Recovery is very quick (max 50 frames). Will be on when standing at night with no headlights.";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Frozen_Windshield_Lens_0 "Significant failsafe indicating windshield is frozen. This will impact on all technologies.";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_Out_Of_Focus_0 "Vision detected that the focus calibration is not correct.";
CM_ SG_ 369 FS_C2C_Out_Of_Calib_0 "Vision detected that  reported  camera to main  camera  calibration, can't be corrected (Auto Fix).";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Protocol_Version "Denotes protocol version";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Sync_ID_0 "Sync ID to be used to sync between signals in system";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Adjacent_Count "Maximum number of lines supported by this protocol";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Lane_Track_ID_0 "ID of the lane mark model. Each lane mark has its own unique ID which is kept as long as the lane mark is tracked.";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Age_0 "The age represents the duration of the lane mark from the first frame it was detected.";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Confidence_0 "The confidence indicates the probability that the lane mark actually exists.";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Color_0 "The color classification of the lane mark;  can be white, yellow or blue";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Color_Conf_0 "The confidence of the lane mark color classification";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Prediction_Reason_0 "Prediction_Reason [i] will be set to true if the lane mark was predicted for reason i  more than one index of the array might be set to true, since several predictions can be activated simultaneously(first segment only)";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Availability_State_0 "The lane mark can be detected, predicted or unavailable. The lane mark is considered predicted only if no segment is detected from the image.  Not availble for Rear camera";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_View_Range_Start_0 "The lane mark polynomial should be used only between VR start to VR end. VR start represents the first point detected or predicted, the smaller between the two.";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_View_Range_End_0 "The lane mark polynomial should be used only between VR start to VR end. VR end represents the last point detected or predicted, the larger between the two. The negative values support the signals from the rear camera (converted to the front camera coordinate system)";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Measured_VR_End_0 "Measured view range indicates the furthest detected point. Measured view range is always smaller or equal to VR end. The negative values support the signals from the rear camera (converted to the front camera coordinate system)";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Lanemark_Type_0 "The type classification of the lane mark.  The double lane mark (DLM) type have sub-type; see LA_DLM_Type. HOV and decceleration types are not supported for the next lanes. The negative values support the signals from the rear camera (converted to the front camera coordinate system)";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_DLM_Type_0 "Double lane mark type is defined first by the inner lane mark (close to the vehicle) and than the outer lane mark.";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Lanemark_Type_Conf_0 "The confidence of the lane mark type classification";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Line_Side_0 "The role of the lane mark relative to the host vehicle.  Commonly the host left boundary is also the right boundary of the next left lane (and the host right boundary is also the left boundary of the next right lane)  In safety zone (hatched area) there are two lane marks that defines the next lane.   For next lane to the right of the host lane: the RIGHT_LEFT_LANEMARK is the closer line to the host lane and the RIGHT_RIGHT_LANEMARK is the further.   When no safety zone, one of the lane mark is defined by the host line and the second is by the following: RIGHT_RIGHT_LANEMARK represents the next lane mark to the right of the host, LEFT_LEFT_LANEMARK represents the next lane mark to the left of the host.";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Marker_Width_0 "The lane mark width is defined as the distance between the inner most edge of the inner most lane mark (with respect to vehicles driving in that lane) and the outer most edge of the outer most lane mark. The definition is also valid for multiple lane marks. The width outputted is the lane mark's average width over the lane boundary detected range.";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Marker_Width_STD_0 "Standard deviation of the lane mark width";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Line_C3_0 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Line_C2_0 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Line_C1_0 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'";
CM_ SG_ 396 LA_Line_C0_0 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'";
CM_ SG_ 397 LA_Sync_ID_1 "Sync ID to be used to sync between signals in system";
CM_ SG_ 397 LA_Lane_Track_ID_1 "ID of the lane mark model. Each lane mark has its own unique ID which is kept as long as the lane mark is tracked.";
CM_ SG_ 397 LA_Age_1 "The age represents the duration of the lane mark from the first frame it was detected.";
CM_ SG_ 397 LA_Confidence_1 "The confidence indicates the probability that the lane mark actually exists.";
CM_ SG_ 397 LA_Color_1 "The color classification of the lane mark;  can be white, yellow or blue";
CM_ SG_ 397 LA_Color_Conf_1 "The confidence of the lane mark color classification";
CM_ SG_ 397 LA_Prediction_Reason_1 "Prediction_Reason [i] will be set to true if the lane mark was predicted for reason i  more than one index of the array might be set to true, since several predictions can be activated simultaneously(first segment only)";
CM_ SG_ 397 LA_Availability_State_1 "The lane mark can be detected, predicted or unavailable. The lane mark is considered predicted only if no segment is detected from the image.  Not availble for Rear camera";
CM_ SG_ 397 LA_View_Range_Start_1 "The lane mark polynomial should be used only between VR start to VR end. VR start represents the first point detected or predicted, the smaller between the two.";
CM_ SG_ 397 LA_View_Range_End_1 "The lane mark polynomial should be used only between VR start to VR end. VR end represents the last point detected or predicted, the larger between the two. The negative values support the signals from the rear camera (converted to the front camera coordinate system)";
CM_ SG_ 397 LA_Measured_VR_End_1 "Measured view range indicates the furthest detected point. Measured view range is always smaller or equal to VR end. The negative values support the signals from the rear camera (converted to the front camera coordinate system)";
CM_ SG_ 397 LA_Lanemark_Type_1 "The type classification of the lane mark.  The double lane mark (DLM) type have sub-type; see LA_DLM_Type. HOV and decceleration types are not supported for the next lanes. The negative values support the signals from the rear camera (converted to the front camera coordinate system)";
CM_ SG_ 397 LA_DLM_Type_1 "Double lane mark type is defined first by the inner lane mark (close to the vehicle) and than the outer lane mark.";
CM_ SG_ 397 LA_Lanemark_Type_Conf_1 "The confidence of the lane mark type classification";
CM_ SG_ 397 LA_Line_Side_1 "The role of the lane mark relative to the host vehicle.  Commonly the host left boundary is also the right boundary of the next left lane (and the host right boundary is also the left boundary of the next right lane)  In safety zone (hatched area) there are two lane marks that defines the next lane.   For next lane to the right of the host lane: the RIGHT_LEFT_LANEMARK is the closer line to the host lane and the RIGHT_RIGHT_LANEMARK is the further.   When no safety zone, one of the lane mark is defined by the host line and the second is by the following: RIGHT_RIGHT_LANEMARK represents the next lane mark to the right of the host, LEFT_LEFT_LANEMARK represents the next lane mark to the left of the host.";
CM_ SG_ 397 LA_Marker_Width_1 "The lane mark width is defined as the distance between the inner most edge of the inner most lane mark (with respect to vehicles driving in that lane) and the outer most edge of the outer most lane mark. The definition is also valid for multiple lane marks. The width outputted is the lane mark's average width over the lane boundary detected range.";
