CM_ SG_ 398 LH_Marker_Width_0 "The lane mark width is defined as the distance between the inner most edge of the inner most lane mark (with respect to vehicles driving in that lane) and the outer most edge of the outer most lane mark. The definition is also valid for multiple lane marks. The width outputted is the lane mark's average width over the lane boundary detected range.";
CM_ SG_ 398 LH_Marker_Width_STD_0 "Standard deviation of the lane mark width";
CM_ SG_ 398 Reserved_4 "Indicate if the Dash Average information is Available (first segment only and on Front Camera Only)";
CM_ SG_ 398 LH_Is_Multi_Clothoid_0 "The lane mark model can be represented by two consecutive segments; first segment and second segment. This representation is rare and needed only in certain scenarios where a single model cannot represent the lane mark accuratly. In those cases, this signal is turned on. Lane mark attributes, like color, type, LM width etc are relevant to the first segment only.";
CM_ SG_ 398 LH_Line_First_C0_0 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'.  In multi-clothoid modeling, this represent the C0 of the first segment coefficient. For single model, the C0 coefficient is used to represent the entire model.";
CM_ SG_ 398 LH_Line_First_C1_0 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'.  In multi-clothoid modeling, this represent the C1 of the first segment coefficient. For single model, the C0 coefficient is used to represent the entire model.";
CM_ SG_ 398 LH_Line_First_C2_0 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'.  In multi-clothoid modeling, this represent the C2 of the first segment coefficient. For single model, the C0 coefficient is used to represent the entire model.";
CM_ SG_ 398 LH_Line_First_C3_0 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'.  In multi-clothoid modeling, this represent the C3 of the first segment coefficient. For single model, the C0 coefficient is used to represent the entire model.";
CM_ SG_ 398 LH_First_VR_Start_0 "The lane mark polynomial should be used only between VR start to VR end. VR start represents the first point detected or predicted, the smaller between the two. In case of multi-chlotoid representation, this is the start VR of the first segment, otherwise (single model) this is the VR start of the model.";
CM_ SG_ 398 LH_First_VR_End_0 "The lane mark polynomial should be used only between VR start to VR end. VR end represents the last point detected or predicted, the larger between the two. In case of multi-chlotoid representation, this is the VR end of the first segment, otherwise (single model) this is the VR end of the model.";
CM_ SG_ 398 LH_First_Measured_VR_End_0 "Measured view range indicates the furthest detected point. Measured view range is always smaller or equal to VR end. Relevant only when model representation is by a single model.  (not relevant for multi-chlotoid modeling)";
CM_ SG_ 398 LH_Second_Measured_VR_End_0 "Measured view range indicates the furthest detected point. Measured view range is always smaller or equal to VR end.  (not relevant for multi-chlotoid modeling)";
CM_ SG_ 398 LH_Line_Second_C0_0 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'.  In multi-clothoid modeling, this represent the C0 of the second segment coefficient. For single modeling, those coefficients are not relevant.";
CM_ SG_ 398 LH_Line_Second_C1_0 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'.  In multi-clothoid modeling, this represent the C1 of the second segment coefficient. For single modeling, those coefficients are not relevant.";
CM_ SG_ 398 LH_Line_Second_C2_0 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'.  In multi-clothoid modeling, this represent the C2 of the second segment coefficient. For single modeling, those coefficients are not relevant.";
CM_ SG_ 398 LH_Line_Second_C3_0 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'.  In multi-clothoid modeling, this represent the C3 of the second segment coefficient. For single modeling, those coefficients are not relevant.";
CM_ SG_ 398 LH_Second_VR_Start_0 "The lane mark polynomial should be used only between VR start to VR end. VR start represents the first point detected or predicted, the smaller between the two. In case of multi-chlotoid representation, this is the start VR of the second segment (not relevant for a single modeling)";
CM_ SG_ 398 LH_Second_VR_End_0 "The lane mark polynomial should be used only between VR start to VR end. VR end represents the last point detected or predicted, the larger between the two. In case of multi-chlotoid representation, this is the VR end of the second segment. (not relevant for a single modeling)";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Sync_ID_1 "Sync ID to be used to sync between signals in system";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_CRC_1 "Calculated over all element signals. From the signal after the CRC until the first signal in the next elements LH_CRC_N+1  not including";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Is_Triggered_SDM_Type_1 "This flag is turned on when the SDM is triggered on lane mark type.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Is_Triggered_SDM_Model_1 "This flag is turned on when the SDM is triggered on lane mark model.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Track_ID_1 "ID of the lane mark model. Each lane mark had its own unique ID which is kept as long as the lane mark is tracked.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Age_1 "The age represents the duration of the lane mark from the first frame it was detected.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Confidence_1 "The confidence indicates the probability that the lane mark actually exists.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Prediction_Reason_1 "Prediction_Reason [i] will be set to true if the lane mark was predicted for reason i  more than one index of the array might be set to true, since several predictions can be actived simultaneously. (This is valid for the first segment only)";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Availability_State_1 "The lane mark can be detected, predicted or unavailable. The lane mark is considered predicted only if no segment is detected from the image.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Color_1 "The color classification of the lane mark;  can be white, yellow or blue";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Color_Confidence_1 "The confidence of the lane mark color classification";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Lanemark_Type_1 "The type classification of the lane mark. The double lane mark (DLM) and the decceleration types have sub-type; see LH_DLM_Type & LH_DECEL_Type";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_DLM_Type_1 "Double lane mark type is defined first by the inner lane mark (close to the vehicle) and than the outer lane mark.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_DECEL_Type_1 "The decceleration area type is defined by the type of the center lane mark.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Lanemark_Type_Conf_1 "The confidence of the lane mark type classification";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Side_1 "The side of the host lane mark ; host left ot host right";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Crossing_1 "The crossing signal is an indication of whether the host vehicle performed lane crossing";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Marker_Width_1 "The lane mark width is defined as the distance between the inner most edge of the inner most lane mark (with respect to vehicles driving in that lane) and the outer most edge of the outer most lane mark. The definition is also valid for multiple lane marks. The width outputted is the lane mark's average width over the lane boundary detected range.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Marker_Width_STD_1 "Standard deviation of the lane mark width";
CM_ SG_ 399 Reserved_5 "Indicate if the Dash Average information is Available (first segment only and on Front Camera Only)";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Is_Multi_Clothoid_1 "The lane mark model can be represented by two consecutive segments; first segment and second segment. This representation is rare and needed only in certain scenarios where a single model cannot represent the lane mark accuratly. In those cases, this signal is turned on. Lane mark attributes, like color, type, LM width etc are relevant to the first segment only.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Line_First_C0_1 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'.  In multi-clothoid modeling, this represent the C0 of the first segment coefficient. For single model, the C0 coefficient is used to represent the entire model.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Line_First_C1_1 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'.  In multi-clothoid modeling, this represent the C1 of the first segment coefficient. For single model, the C0 coefficient is used to represent the entire model.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Line_First_C2_1 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'.  In multi-clothoid modeling, this represent the C2 of the first segment coefficient. For single model, the C0 coefficient is used to represent the entire model.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Line_First_C3_1 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'.  In multi-clothoid modeling, this represent the C3 of the first segment coefficient. For single model, the C0 coefficient is used to represent the entire model.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_First_VR_Start_1 "The lane mark polynomial should be used only between VR start to VR end. VR start represents the first point detected or predicted, the smaller between the two. In case of multi-chlotoid representation, this is the start VR of the first segment, otherwise (single model) this is the VR start of the model.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_First_VR_End_1 "The lane mark polynomial should be used only between VR start to VR end. VR end represents the last point detected or predicted, the larger between the two. In case of multi-chlotoid representation, this is the VR end of the first segment, otherwise (single model) this is the VR end of the model.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_First_Measured_VR_End_1 "Measured view range indicates the furthest detected point. Measured view range is always smaller or equal to VR end. Relevant only when model representation is by a single model.  (not relevant for multi-chlotoid modeling)";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Second_Measured_VR_End_1 "Measured view range indicates the furthest detected point. Measured view range is always smaller or equal to VR end.  (not relevant for multi-chlotoid modeling)";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Line_Second_C0_1 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'.  In multi-clothoid modeling, this represent the C0 of the second segment coefficient. For single modeling, those coefficients are not relevant.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Line_Second_C1_1 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'.  In multi-clothoid modeling, this represent the C1 of the second segment coefficient. For single modeling, those coefficients are not relevant.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Line_Second_C2_1 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'.  In multi-clothoid modeling, this represent the C2 of the second segment coefficient. For single modeling, those coefficients are not relevant.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Line_Second_C3_1 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i'.  In multi-clothoid modeling, this represent the C3 of the second segment coefficient. For single modeling, those coefficients are not relevant.";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Second_VR_Start_1 "The lane mark polynomial should be used only between VR start to VR end. VR start represents the first point detected or predicted, the smaller between the two. In case of multi-chlotoid representation, this is the start VR of the second segment (not relevant for a single modeling)";
CM_ SG_ 399 LH_Second_VR_End_1 "The lane mark polynomial should be used only between VR start to VR end. VR end represents the last point detected or predicted, the larger between the two. In case of multi-chlotoid representation, this is the VR end of the second segment. (not relevant for a single modeling)";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_Header_CRC "Calculated over all header signals. From the signal after the CRC until the first signal in the elements LRE_Element_CRC_0 not including";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_Protocol_Version "Denotes the protocol version";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_Sync_ID_0 "The ID of the Sync message, used to synchronize between signals in the system. Every new frame promotes the sync ID by one.";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_Count "Number of lines reported. Front camera can output up to 4 road edges:one road edge for each side and another road edge for each side if the multiple RE package is enabled. Rear camera can output up to one road edge per each side.";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_Element_CRC_0 "Calculated over all element signals. From the signal after the CRC until the first signal in the next elements LRE_Element_CRC_N+1  not including";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_ID_0 "ID of the lane boundary model. Each lane boundary has its own unique ID which is kept as long as the lane boundary is tracked.";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_Age_0 "The age represents the duration of the lane boundary from the first frame it was detected.";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_Confidence_0 "The Confidence of the road edge. Normally values of the confidence is 0 to 1. When confidence is -1 it means that the confidence is not applicable. As oppose to low value of confidence, it does not implicate on the quality of the road edge model.";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_Prediction_Reason_0 "Prediction_Reason [i] will be set to true if the lane mark was predicted for reason i  more than one index of the array might be set to true, since several predictions can be activated simultaneously(first segment only)";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_Availability_State_0 "The lane boundary can be detected, predicted or unavailable. The lane boundary is considered predicted only if no segment is detected from the image.";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_View_Range_Start_0 "The lane boundary polynomial should be used only between VR start to VR end. VR start represents the first point detected or predicted, the smaller between the two.";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_View_Range_End_0 "The lane boundary polynomial should be used only between VR start to VR end. VR end represents the last point detected or predicted, the larger between the two.";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_Measured_VR_End_0 "Measured view range indicates the furthest detected point. Measured view range is always smaller or equal to VR end.";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_Side_0 "Indicates whether the road edge is at the left or right side of the host vehicle";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_Is_Triggered_SDM_Model_0 "This flag is turned on when the SDM is triggered on lane mark model.";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_Line_C3_0 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i' in the road edge polynomial.";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_Line_C2_0 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i' in the road edge polynomial.";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_Line_C1_0 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i' in the road edge polynomial.";
CM_ SG_ 394 LRE_Line_C0_0 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i' in the road edge polynomial.";
CM_ SG_ 394 Reserved_6 "Place holder for multiple road edge support. The second road edge is supported only for the front camera.";
CM_ SG_ 395 LRE_Sync_ID_1 "The ID of the Sync message, used to synchronize between signals in the system. Every new frame promotes the sync ID by one.";
CM_ SG_ 395 LRE_Element_CRC_1 "Calculated over all element signals. From the signal after the CRC until the first signal in the next elements LRE_Element_CRC_N+1  not including";
CM_ SG_ 395 LRE_ID_1 "ID of the lane boundary model. Each lane boundary has its own unique ID which is kept as long as the lane boundary is tracked.";
CM_ SG_ 395 LRE_Age_1 "The age represents the duration of the lane boundary from the first frame it was detected.";
CM_ SG_ 395 LRE_Confidence_1 "The Confidence of the road edge. Normally values of the confidence is 0 to 1. When confidence is -1 it means that the confidence is not applicable. As oppose to low value of confidence, it does not implicate on the quality of the road edge model.";
CM_ SG_ 395 LRE_Prediction_Reason_1 "Prediction_Reason [i] will be set to true if the lane mark was predicted for reason i  more than one index of the array might be set to true, since several predictions can be activated simultaneously(first segment only)";
CM_ SG_ 395 LRE_Availability_State_1 "The lane boundary can be detected, predicted or unavailable. The lane boundary is considered predicted only if no segment is detected from the image.";
CM_ SG_ 395 LRE_View_Range_Start_1 "The lane boundary polynomial should be used only between VR start to VR end. VR start represents the first point detected or predicted, the smaller between the two.";
CM_ SG_ 395 LRE_View_Range_End_1 "The lane boundary polynomial should be used only between VR start to VR end. VR end represents the last point detected or predicted, the larger between the two.";
CM_ SG_ 395 LRE_Measured_VR_End_1 "Measured view range indicates the furthest detected point. Measured view range is always smaller or equal to VR end. Currently, for the supported RE prediction types, the LRE_Measured_VR_End will always be equal to LRE_View_Range_End.";
CM_ SG_ 395 LRE_Side_1 "Indicates whether the road edge is at the left or right side of the host vehicle";
CM_ SG_ 395 LRE_Is_Triggered_SDM_Model_1 "This flag is turned on when the SDM is triggered on lane mark model.";
CM_ SG_ 395 LRE_Line_C3_1 "Ci is coefficient corresponding to variable with power of 'i' in the road edge polynomial.";
